# ============================================================================
# RETRACTED - DO NOT QUOTE ANY NUMBER IN THIS FILE AS A RESULT.
#
# This RMSD series was computed with `gmx rms` referenced to a .gro file
# (see the "Command line:" header below). Without a run input (.tpr) GROMACS
# cannot make molecules whole across periodic boundaries, so what is plotted
# here is largely periodic-image displacement, not conformational change.
# It is also from the 100 ps check run, not a production trajectory.
#
# The 10.11 A and 14.30 A RMSD figures that came out of this family of check
# runs are WITHDRAWN. Changing only the reference .gro moved the "result" by
# about 14 A, which is what identified the quantity as a PBC artefact: a
# protein that had genuinely moved 24 A would be unfolded, and the hydrogen
# bond, DSSP and radius-of-gyration data flatly contradict that.
#
# These files are kept, labelled, so the correction stays visible rather than
# disappearing. The correct System B backbone RMSD is in
# ../system_B/reduced_bb_rmsd.xvg (production trajectory, .tpr-referenced,
# PBC-corrected). See ../../docs/RETRACTIONS.md.
